# Intention and botanical safety

Read before changing intention, session-readiness, reminder, locality, botanical, supplement, evidence or discovery behavior:

- `docs/requirements/INTENTION_AND_BOTANICAL_SCOPE_ADDENDUM.md`
- `docs/architecture/INTENTION_AND_BOTANICAL_THREE_TIER_ARCHITECTURE.md`
- `docs/security/BOTANICAL_SAFETY_AND_LOCATION_PRIVACY_RULES.md`
- `docs/decisions/ADR-SCOPE-INT-BOT-001.md`

Required:

- use attention-regulation and deliberate-practice language; do not claim mind control;
- keep intention text private by default and out of general logs/outbox payloads;
- model reminders deterministically with snooze/disable and duplicate-delivery handling;
- treat botanical occurrence, seasonality and traditional use as separate from safety and efficacy;
- require exact taxon, plant part, preparation and evidence version;
- never transfer dosage across preparations, extracts or concentrations;
- use coarse locality by default and suppress sensitive/protected-species coordinates;
- fail closed when identity, legal status, evidence, interaction or safety review is incomplete;
- Project B consumes only a published Canonical projection and cannot write botanical evidence;
- no autonomous publication, individualized dosage or unreviewed foraging instruction in the curated pilot;
- do not implement this scope until an accepted successor packet explicitly authorizes it.
